title: Colors, 2D Transforms and filters
intro: A color picker on every color field, the Transform in 2D, and filters to find a field or an entity fast.
project: Platformer | Inspector Tools

chapter: Filters | Find a field, or an entity, by typing
select: Player
say: The player has seven components and nearly fifty fields. Say you want its speeds.
click: filter:fields
type: speed
expectmatches: fields = 6
explain: panel:Inspector | Speeds | Type in the filter at the top of the Inspector, and only the fields with speed in their names are left, under their subheadings, folded or not.
say: It stays as you pick other entities, so you can compare one field across them. Escape clears it.
key: Escape
click: filter:entities
type: coin
expectmatches: entities = 9
explain: panel:Hierarchy | Coins | The Hierarchy has one too. Every coin shows, with what it sits inside opened and drawn faintly, so you can see where each one is.
key: Escape
say: Clear it, and the tree goes back the way it was.

chapter: Transforms in 2D | X and Y, and one angle
expectaxes: Transform.Position = X, Y
expectaxes: Transform.Rotation = Z
explain: component:Transform | Transform | Griff games are mostly flat, so the Transform shows position and scale in X and Y, and rotation as one angle.
set: Transform.Rotation.Z = 15
expectvalue: Player.Transform.Rotation.Z = 15
set: Transform.Rotation.Z = 0
explain: transform:3d | 3D | Making something in 3D? This switch shows Z as well, on every entity, and the editor remembers it.
click: transform:3d
expectaxes: Transform.Position = X, Y, Z
expectaxes: Transform.Rotation = X, Y, Z
wait: 1
click: transform:3d
expectaxes: Transform.Position = X, Y

chapter: Colors | A picker on every color field
explain: color:Sprite.Tint | Tint | Color fields used to take a hex code and nothing else. Now the swatch opens a picker.
click: color:Sprite.Tint
explain: color:square | Strength and brightness | Drag across the square for how strong the color is, and up it for how bright.
colordrag: hue = 200
say: The strip below picks the hue. The player changes as you drag.
colordrag: square = 0.75, 0.9
colordrag: alpha = 0.6
say: And this one makes it see through.
explain: color:swatches | Palette | Underneath is the Sprite Painter's palette, so your sprites and tints come from the same colors.
click: color:pick:#29ADFF
expectvalue: Player.Sprite.Tint = #29ADFF
click: color:Sprite.Tint
select: Slime
click: color:Sprite.Tint
explain: color:recent | Recent | And colors you picked lately are kept, in every color field, for next time.
click: color:pick:#29ADFF
expectvalue: Slime.Sprite.Tint = #29ADFF
click: color:Sprite.Tint
say: Each drag or pick is one undo step, and it works on everything selected at once. Agents get the same picker, filters and 3D switch through the Inspector.
